1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,170
Shifts brings two kinds of scheduling into
one place.

2
00:00:03,589 --> 00:00:06,619
Recurring Group Shifts organizes people
and required

3
00:00:06,650 --> 00:00:08,529
roles across dated shift days.

4
00:00:08,949 --> 00:00:12,880
Add Static Shift creates a separate fixed
window for resources.

5
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:15,920
Start by identifying the work you need to
coordinate.

6
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:20,319
In our fictional Chicago Fire department,
we will create an assigned personnel

7
00:00:20,319 --> 00:00:22,940
schedule, then a separate signup schedule.

8
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:28,530
Your Shifts, On Duty Now, Approvals and
Shift Staffing are separate views.

9
00:00:28,950 --> 00:00:32,509
A scheduled roster gives you recorded
coverage; check current

10
00:00:32,509 --> 00:00:34,430
operational information separately.

11
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:37,859
Choose Add Recurring Group Shift to open
New Shift.

12
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:43,259
Enter a distinctive practice name and the
short code T R N twenty-eight A.

13
00:00:43,709 --> 00:00:46,900
Assignment Type is Assigned, so the
administrator chooses

14
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:48,299
the people for this schedule.

15
00:00:48,730 --> 00:00:52,060
Use a light background color because the
calendar text is black.

16
00:00:52,469 --> 00:00:55,769
The supervisor approval checkbox is clear
in this example.

17
00:00:56,139 --> 00:01:00,900
That control governs signups and trades;
it is not the list of assigned personnel.

18
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:04,769
Review these choices before using Next to
open Schedule.

19
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:08,450
Schedule gives you a multi-month date
picker and separate Start

20
00:01:08,450 --> 00:01:10,039
Time and End Time fields.

21
00:01:10,470 --> 00:01:13,859
Our example selects November fourth,
twenty twenty-six, from

22
00:01:13,859 --> 00:01:15,449
nine to eleven in the morning.

23
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,380
Check both displayed times after leaving
the fields and confirm

24
00:01:19,380 --> 00:01:20,990
the intended date is highlighted.

25
00:01:21,419 --> 00:01:24,779
This is a manually selected schedule, even
though it appears

26
00:01:24,779 --> 00:01:26,289
under Recurring Group Shifts.

27
00:01:26,599 --> 00:01:29,830
The wizard shown here does not offer a
rotation preset.

28
00:01:30,289 --> 00:01:33,849
Once the date and times are correct,
continue to the Slots stage.

29
00:01:34,029 --> 00:01:37,210
In Slots, Add Group to Shift adds a group
row.

30
00:01:37,630 --> 00:01:39,750
Firehouse fifty-one is selected here.

31
00:01:40,219 --> 00:01:43,909
Add Role to Group creates a required-role
row for that group.

32
00:01:44,399 --> 00:01:47,250
Choose Officer and leave Roles Count at
one.

33
00:01:47,689 --> 00:01:50,239
These values define what coverage the
schedule should

34
00:01:50,239 --> 00:01:51,780
compare against its roster.

35
00:01:52,190 --> 00:01:54,840
Adding a role minimum does not assign a
person.

36
00:01:55,290 --> 00:01:59,559
Review the group, role and count together,
then continue to Personnel.

37
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,030
Use the department’s published role
conventions when configuring

38
00:02:03,030 --> 00:02:04,700
your own coverage requirements.

39
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:08,999
Personnel separates Non-Group Personnel
from the individual group pickers.

40
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:12,959
Non-group entries are described as
floaters or standbys.

41
00:02:13,510 --> 00:02:16,909
In the Firehouse fifty-one picker, choose
Matthew Casey.

42
00:02:17,329 --> 00:02:19,529
His selected name is visible as a chip.

43
00:02:20,010 --> 00:02:23,109
Leave the other group pickers empty for
this small exercise.

44
00:02:23,609 --> 00:02:27,209
The text explains that assigned people
fill role slots according

45
00:02:27,209 --> 00:02:28,550
to their group and roles.

46
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:33,000
Verify the selected member under the
intended group; selecting a name

47
00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:34,820
elsewhere is a different assignment.

48
00:02:35,289 --> 00:02:37,450
Use Next when that review is complete.

49
00:02:37,679 --> 00:02:40,939
The Finish stage contains an instruction
and a separate Finish

50
00:02:40,939 --> 00:02:42,420
control at the lower right.

51
00:02:42,779 --> 00:02:44,869
That lower control creates the schedule.

52
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:48,969
Submit once and read the returned row in
Recurring Group Shifts.

53
00:02:49,370 --> 00:02:53,659
Our new row says Assigned and Manual, with
one group and one person.

54
00:02:54,089 --> 00:02:58,890
It offers View Calendar, Edit Details,
Edit Calendar and Edit Groups.

55
00:02:59,190 --> 00:03:02,210
Those actions inspect different parts of
the saved schedule.

56
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:06,669
Confirm the new row before opening an
editor or assuming that a prepared

57
00:03:06,669 --> 00:03:08,300
wizard has already been stored.

58
00:03:08,550 --> 00:03:13,179
Reopen Edit Details to check the stored
name, code, light blue color

59
00:03:13,249 --> 00:03:15,010
and nine-to-eleven time window.

60
00:03:15,409 --> 00:03:18,179
Casey remains selected under Firehouse
fifty-one.

61
00:03:18,820 --> 00:03:21,830
In the shared calendar, open the November
fourth entry.

62
00:03:22,219 --> 00:03:25,529
Its day detail is Upcoming and shows the
same times.

63
00:03:25,939 --> 00:03:29,910
The Officer row says Required one and
Needed zero; the

64
00:03:29,910 --> 00:03:32,189
roster lists Casey as Assigned.

65
00:03:32,689 --> 00:03:36,389
Fully staffed means this configured
one-role requirement is filled.

66
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:39,900
It does not establish arrival,
qualifications or

67
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:41,299
an apparatus crew assignment.

68
00:03:41,770 --> 00:03:44,200
Read the actual role counts behind the
summary.

69
00:03:44,399 --> 00:03:49,410
For a signup schedule, create a separate
practice entry with code T R N

70
00:03:49,519 --> 00:03:52,549
twenty-eight S and Assignment Type Signup.

71
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:56,330
Check Signups and trades need supervisor
approval.

72
00:03:56,729 --> 00:04:00,680
The help says that a signup or trade does
not put anyone on duty until

73
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:02,410
a group supervisor approves it.

74
00:04:02,850 --> 00:04:07,340
Select November fifth and sixth, using the
same morning time window and one

75
00:04:07,340 --> 00:04:09,609
required Officer for Firehouse fifty-one.

76
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:12,139
Leave every Personnel picker empty.

77
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:14,820
Members can request their own dates
separately.

78
00:04:15,279 --> 00:04:18,159
Review Finish and submit this new schedule
once.

79
00:04:18,379 --> 00:04:21,260
The saved row now carries Approval
required.

80
00:04:21,679 --> 00:04:27,009
Reopen its details and calendar to verify
the setting, times and two selected dates.

81
00:04:27,490 --> 00:04:31,139
On November fifth, the day detail is
Signup and Upcoming.

82
00:04:31,469 --> 00:04:34,979
It shows Open slots one, an Officer
requirement of one,

83
00:04:35,299 --> 00:04:37,299
and Nobody is on this day yet.

84
00:04:37,660 --> 00:04:41,219
Your Status says that the current user is
not on this day, and a

85
00:04:41,219 --> 00:04:42,979
group signup button is available.

86
00:04:43,340 --> 00:04:47,410
An empty roster remains unfilled even
though the schedule has been created.

87
00:04:47,779 --> 00:04:51,739
A member request and its supervisor review
are separate operations.

88
00:04:51,949 --> 00:04:56,550
Department Shift Settings has a separate
Allow Signups For Multiple Groups option.

89
00:04:57,030 --> 00:04:59,349
It is off here and remains unchanged.

90
00:04:59,769 --> 00:05:03,810
The help asks you to review overlaps and
local coverage rules separately.

91
00:05:04,260 --> 00:05:06,909
This department policy is different from
the approval

92
00:05:06,909 --> 00:05:08,920
checkbox on an individual shift.

93
00:05:09,450 --> 00:05:13,760
Open Approvals to review waiting signups
and trades in groups you supervise.

94
00:05:14,170 --> 00:05:16,149
Both queues are empty in this example.

95
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:19,950
The page states that a pending request
does not put anyone

96
00:05:19,950 --> 00:05:21,790
on duty until it is approved.

97
00:05:22,190 --> 00:05:24,859
An empty queue is not a completed
approval.

98
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:28,089
On Duty Now shows a timestamp and the
currently active

99
00:05:28,089 --> 00:05:29,869
shift, grouped by assignment.

100
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:34,790
Here the existing A Shift is active, with
its recorded members and roles.

101
00:05:35,210 --> 00:05:37,689
Our new November dates are future
schedules.

102
00:05:38,050 --> 00:05:41,960
Keep those two questions separate: who is
scheduled on a selected day,

103
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:44,009
and which schedule is active now.

104
00:05:44,439 --> 00:05:48,320
The page says it refreshes every minute
and also offers Refresh.

105
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:53,009
These are recorded roster views; use the
appropriate operational workflow

106
00:05:53,009 --> 00:05:56,800
to verify current availability and other
information your team needs.

107
00:05:56,880 --> 00:06:00,560
Chicago Fire can use this pattern to
coordinate station coverage.

108
00:06:00,979 --> 00:06:04,539
Community care and mental health teams can
schedule operational team

109
00:06:04,539 --> 00:06:06,419
coverage without patient detail.

110
00:06:06,770 --> 00:06:11,109
Search and rescue can organize standby
roles; security teams can coordinate

111
00:06:11,109 --> 00:06:16,029
site coverage; wildland crews can plan
relief rosters; and industrial response

112
00:06:16,029 --> 00:06:17,750
teams can schedule drill support.

113
00:06:18,230 --> 00:06:22,019
In every setting, choose the right
assignment type, state the group

114
00:06:22,050 --> 00:06:26,199
and role requirements clearly, and verify
the saved dated roster.

115
00:06:26,630 --> 00:06:30,389
Handle member requests, approvals,
attendance and trades through

116
00:06:30,389 --> 00:06:31,999
their own reviewed steps.

